      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "An arithmetic sequence $f(n)$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)-7,\\,f(1)=4,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nWhat is the $4$th term of the sequence?",
      "worked_solution": "Starting with the first term $f(1)=4,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive rule until we reach the $4$th term $f(4).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =4 \\\\ f(2) & =f(1)-7=4-7=-3 \\\\ f(3) & =f(2)-7=-3-7=-10 \\\\ f(4) & =f(3)-7=-10-7=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $4$th term is $f(4)=-17.$",
